  "five_key_questions": {
    "Q1_meaningful_improvement": "YES \u2014 meaningful improvement in most metrics. Experiment A accuracy: 0.9956 vs baseline 0.4768. Low recall in A: 1.0000 vs baseline 0.0000. Leakage-free (C) Low recall: 0.3130 \u2014 this is the honest signal.",
    "Q2_leakage_or_better_labels": "BOTH. Experiment A (includes wpm, pause_count) accuracy=0.9956, Low recall=1.0000. Experiment C (leakage-free, only speech_duration + word_count) accuracy=0.4538, Low recall=0.3130. The gap between A and C is the target leakage contribution. Genuine signal from independent features is limited.",
    "Q3_useful_features": "In Experiment A: top features by importance: [('pause_count', 0.4594), ('wpm', 0.3177), ('speech_duration', 0.2069), ('word_count', 0.016)]. In leakage-free C: [('speech_duration', 0.6474), ('word_count', 0.3526)]. wpm and pause_count dominate in A/B because they directly encode the labeling rule. speech_duration and word_count are the only genuinely independent predictors.",
    "Q4_safe_for_hackathon": "YES \u2014 safe for a hackathon prototype.",
    "Q5_limitations_to_disclose": "1. TARGET LEAKAGE: Labels were generated using wpm and pause_count; these same features are in the model \u2014 Experiment A/B accuracy is inflated by rule-memorization. 2. RULE-GENERATED LABELS: Ground truth is domain rules, not human perceptual judgment of hesitation. The model learns a rule approximation, not real hesitation. 3. LIMITED INDEPENDENT SIGNAL: Leakage-free features (speech_duration, word_count) alone have low discriminative power \u2014 real hesitation depends on prosody, disfluencies, and fill words that are not captured in this dataset. 4. CLASS IMBALANCE REMAINS: High is ~62% of candidate dataset \u2014 model will still naturally prefer High. 5. NO HUMAN LABELS: Dataset has no perceptually validated Low/High hesitation samples. 6. INFERENCE PIPELINE GAP: Production inference (audio_features.py) already computes pause_count and wpm, so the feature gap is bridgeable \u2014 but label quality remains the fundamental constraint."
  }
